# chain position): "AN:NTER" is AMBER's NALA nitrogen, an ammonium N3 at
# +0.1414 e, where "AN" is ALA's amide N at -0.4157 e. amber.grp's :NTER and
# :CTER rules ask for these by name (ReduceRule::forcefield_key), and a force
# field that does not carry them falls back on the unqualified type and says
# so -- so an old .ff paired with a new .grp degrades to today's charges rather
# than to particles with no mass.
#
# Charges are AMBER's own, from the NXXX/CXXX templates. Radius, epsilon, mass
# and transfer energy are the interior type's, unless AMBER changes the atom's
# class -- which it does only for N -> N3, HA's H1 -> HP and O -> O2 -- in
# which case they come from that class. Copying rather than recomputing is what
# carries the three deliberate deviations in this file (SHG, THG1, YHH, see the
# note at the top) onto their terminal twins. Hydrophobicity is the interior
# type's: where a residue sits does not change its side chain.
#
